.TH "tm" "1" "2026\-11\-10"
.PP
.SH NAME
tm \- universal taskmark utility
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtm\fR <command> [options]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBtm\fR is the command\-line interface for SPEC\-TASKMARK\-05 taskmark files.\& It
provides subcommands for atomic task mutations, compact task listings
addressed by task identifier, sweeping completed tasks between task documents in
strict reverse chronological order, archiving aged\-out sections, validating
files for spec compliance, and filtering arbitrary text into and out of a
payload block.\& The specification it implements is documented in
\fIdoc/taskmark_spec.\&md\fR.\&
.PP
Unless a path is given, \fBtm\fR operates on the \fI.\&tasks\fR directory relative to
the current working directory (the layout described by the spec).\&
.PP
.SH COMMANDS
\fBinit\fR [\-\-orphan [\fIBRANCH\fR]] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Bootstrap \fI.\&tasks\fR with starter \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR, \fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR, and
\fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR files.\& Never overwrites a file that already exists.\&
With \fB\-\-orphan\fR, keeps the tasks directory on its own git branch,
mounted as a worktree (see \fB\-\-orphan\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBsync\fR [\-m \fIMSG\fR] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR] [\-p|\-\-push]
.RS 4
Stage and commit every change in the tasks directory (default message
"tasks: sync (<timestamp>)"), and with \fB\-\-push\fR push it.\& The tasks
directory must be the top level of its own git work tree \-\- normally
the worktree made by \fBinit \-\-orphan\fR \-\- so nothing outside it can be
staged; a plain directory inside a larger repository is refused.\& Git
hooks run as for any commit, and git'\&s own messages are shown when a
commit or push fails.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBlist\fR [\-\-pending|\-\-all] [\-\-not \fITAG\fR].\&.\&.\& [\fITAG\fR.\&.\&.\&] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR] [\fIfile\fR.\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Print one line per task, its handle and summary, e.\&g.\&
"[k7q2x] (A) Task text id:k7q2x", without payload blocks, to keep
listings short for humans and AI agents alike.\& By default, lists pending
tasks from the active task document.\& With \fB\-\-all\fR, lists both pending
and completed tasks (completed tasks marked `[x]`).\& An argument starting
with '\&+'\& or '\&@'\& is a tag: only tasks carrying every \fITAG\fR given, as a
whole word anywhere on the task line, are listed, and \fB\-\-not\fR \fITAG\fR
leaves out tasks carrying it.\& Given several files, each listing
is headed `== <file>`.\& A file with nothing to list prints nothing on
standard output and a short note on standard error.\& A missing file is
an error.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBnext\fR [\-\-not \fITAG\fR].\&.\&.\& [\fITAG\fR.\&.\&.\&] [\-\-file \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Print the task to start, in the format of \fBlist\fR: among the pending
tasks of \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR (or \fB\-\-file\fR) that match the tag filters and
have no unmet dependency, the one with the highest priority flag, or
the first in file order when none is flagged.\& A dependency (see TASK
IDENTIFIERS) is met once the task it names is completed, in any task
file.\& A dependency naming no task counts as unmet and is reported on
standard error.\& When no task is ready, prints nothing on standard
output, a note on standard error, and exits 0.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBadd\fR \fI<task\-text>\fR [\-p|\-\-priority \fIPRI\fR] [\-\-section \fISECTION\fR | \-\-before \fITASK\fR | \-\-after \fITASK\fR] [\-\-file \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Add a pending task at the end of the named section'\&s own content
(before its first subheading), or of the first heading'\&s when no
\fB\-\-section\fR is given; or, with \fB\-\-before\fR or \fB\-\-after\fR, directly above
the named task or directly below its payload, under whatever heading
that task sits.\& An unknown section or a missing file is an error;
no file is ever created.\& \fB\-p A\fR adds the `(A)` priority flag.\& The task
is stamped with a new identifier (see TASK IDENTIFIERS) unless its text
already carries one, such as one carried over from an existing
numbering scheme (`tm add "Fix the parser id:z0114"`); a supplied
identifier that already occurs in any task file is an error.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBid\fR [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR] [\fIfile\fR.\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Stamp a new identifier on every pending task that lacks one, in
\fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR and \fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR or in the files given.\& Completed
tasks are never changed.\& Also reports, on standard error, any
identifier carried by more than one task in any task file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdone\fR \fI<hash\-or\-pattern>\fR [\-\-git [\fIREV\fR]] [\-\-file \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Find a pending task in \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR (or \fB\-\-file\fR) by handle or
substring (see TASK HANDLES), mark it `\- [x]` in place, and stamp a
Completed field with the local date into the leading run of its
labeled fields, adding `git:<sha>` with \fB\-\-git\fR.\& Only pending tasks are
candidates; a match that is already completed is reported as such.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBmove\fR \fI<hash\-or\-pattern>\fR [\-\-from \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-to \fIFILE\fR] [\-\-section \fISECTION\fR | \-\-before \fITASK\fR | \-\-after \fITASK\fR] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Move a task and its payload from one file to another (by default from
\fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR to \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR), or to another place in the same
file, placed as for \fBadd\fR; with \fB\-\-before\fR or \fB\-\-after\fR in one file,
this reorders the queue.\& The destination is written before the task
is removed from the source, so an interrupted move leaves a duplicate,
never a loss.\& The destination must exist.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBsweep\fR
.RS 4
Move every `\- [x]` task and its payload out of \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR and into
\fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR, bucketed under a "## YYYY\-MM" section for the month
of the sweep, or "## Sprint \fILABEL\fR" with \fB\-\-sprint\fR.\& Tasks within a
section and sections within the file are kept in strict reverse chronological
order (newest completed first).\& Headings and top\-level prose in \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR
are never swept, even when every task beneath them is done.\& \fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR
is never read or written.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBarchive\fR
.RS 4
Move sections aged out of \fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR into
\fI.\&tasks/archive/<YYYY>/<YYYY\-MM>.\&tm.\&md\fR, grouped by the month of
each section'\&s most recent \fBCompleted\fR task and inserted newest first
beneath the archive file'\&s title.\& A section is retained if it is among
the 2 newest or its most recent \fBCompleted\fR task is dated within the
last 14 days.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBcheck\-shas\fR [\-\-branch \fIREF\fR] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Report each `git:<sha>` citation in any task file, the archive
included, that does not name a commit in the repository holding the
tasks directory, as \fIfile\fR:\fIline\fR: git:\fIsha\fR \fIreason\fR.\& With \fB\-\-branch\fR,
also report commits not reachable from \fIREF\fR, such as the commits of a
feature branch that was squash\-merged.\& Exits 1 when it reports
anything.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBremap\fR \fIOLD\fR \fINEW\fR [\fIOLD\fR \fINEW\fR.\&.\&.\&] [\-\-tasks\-dir \fIDIR\fR]
.RS 4
Replace every citation of commit \fIOLD\fR \-\- any abbreviation of it, such
as `git:a1b2c3d` for a full \fIOLD\fR \-\- with `git:`\fINEW\fR, in every task
file, the archive and completed tasks included.\& Each \fINEW\fR must name a
commit.\& Prints, per pair, how many citations changed in how many
files, which can go in the message of the task commit that records the
remapping.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBvalidate\fR [\-\-fix] [file.\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Validate taskmark file(s) for SPEC\-TASKMARK\-05 compliance.\& If no \fIfile\fR
is given, defaults to the configured active file.\& If \fB\-\-fix\fR is given,
automatically repairs common formatting errors (over\-indented bullet
continuations and sub\-lists, wrapped labeled fields, missing blank lines
after labeled fields, prose directly beneath a task or payload, hard
tabs, leading frontmatter blocks from pre\-0.\&4 files, and top\-level dash
bullets converted to '\&*'\&).\& The file'\&s newline style is preserved.\& Exits 0 on success (or successful
repair), 1 on validation failure or file error.\&
.PP
Beyond the rules of the specification, prints non\-fatal `[WARN]` lines
that never change the exit status: a \fBCreated\fR, \fBDue\fR, or \fBCompleted\fR
field whose value is not the registered date format; a `**Key:**`
inside a field'\&s value, which is read as text and is usually a second
field written on the same line; and an identifier carried by two tasks
among the files given.\& In a completed task only the \fBCompleted\fR field
is checked: the rest of its text is a record.\& Duplicate identifiers are
looked for only among the files given; \fBid\fR checks every task file.\& Output is coloured only when standard output is
a terminal and the \fBNO_COLOR\fR environment variable is unset or empty.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBindent\fR [info]
.RS 4
Read stdin, prefix every non\-blank line with the four\-space payload
indent, and write the result to stdout.\& Blank lines are emitted
genuinely empty.\& \fIinfo\fR, if given, wraps the result in a fenced code
block carrying that info string.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdedent\fR [\-\-fence]
.RS 4
Read stdin, remove exactly four leading spaces from every non\-blank
line, and write the result to stdout.\& Exits non\-zero rather than
truncate a line that lacks the full four\-space prefix.\& \fB\-\-fence\fR also
drops the first and last line, for lifting a fenced block back out.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBhelp\fR
.RS 4
Show a short usage summary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBversion\fR
.RS 4
Print the version and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
\fB\-\-pending\fR
.RS 4
With \fBlist\fR: output only pending tasks (the default).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-all\fR
.RS 4
With \fBlist\fR: output both pending and completed tasks.\& Completed tasks are
marked with `[x]`.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-not\fR \fITAG\fR
.RS 4
With \fBlist\fR and \fBnext\fR: leave out tasks whose line carries \fITAG\fR
(e.\&g.\& `\-\-not @review`).\& May be repeated.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-priority\fR \fIPRI\fR
.RS 4
With \fBadd\fR: assign a priority flag `(A)`\-`(Z)` to the task.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-section\fR \fISECTION\fR
.RS 4
With \fBadd\fR and \fBmove\fR: heading (matched case\-insensitively) whose own
content the task is appended to.\& Must exist.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Target file to operate on.\& Defaults to the configured active file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-before\fR \fITASK\fR, \fB\-\-after\fR \fITASK\fR
.RS 4
With \fBadd\fR and \fBmove\fR: place the task directly above \fITASK\fR, or directly
below \fITASK\fR'\&s payload.\& \fITASK\fR is a handle or pattern, resolved in the
destination file as for \fBdone\fR.\& Not combined with \fB\-\-section\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fIREF\fR
.RS 4
With \fBcheck\-shas\fR: also report citations of commits not reachable
from \fIREF\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-from\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
With \fBmove\fR: source file to move the task from (defaults to \fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-to\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
With \fBmove\fR: destination file to move the task to (defaults to \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-git\fR [\fIREV\fR]
.RS 4
With \fBdone\fR: record the short SHA of \fIREV\fR (default \fBHEAD\fR) in the
Completed field, e.\&g.\& `> \fB\fRCompleted:\fB\fR YYYY\-MM\-DD git:<sha>`.\& \fIREV\fR
must name a commit in the current repository.\& The word after \fB\-\-git\fR is
taken as \fIREV\fR only when the command would otherwise have two
arguments, so `tm done \-\-git abc1234 parser` and `tm done parser \-\-git`
both work; `\-\-git=`\fIREV\fR is always unambiguous.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-sprint\fR \fILABEL\fR
.RS 4
With \fBsweep\fR: bucket the swept tasks under "## Sprint \fILABEL\fR" instead
of the current month.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Report what would move and change nothing.\& Applies to \fBsweep\fR and
\fBarchive\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-tasks\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory holding the task files.\& Defaults to \fI.\&/.\&tasks\fR, or the
\fBtasks_dir\fR set in \fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR (see CONFIGURATION).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-orphan\fR [\fIBRANCH\fR]
.RS 4
With \fBinit\fR, run from the repository root: mount branch \fIBRANCH\fR
(default \fItasks\fR) at the tasks directory as a git worktree, add the
directory to \fI.\&gitignore\fR (and, when it is not \fI.\&tasks\fR, set \fBtasks_dir\fR in
\fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR).\& An existing local branch is mounted as is; a branch
already fetched from a remote is checked out tracking it, so a
collaborator joins the shared
task history; otherwise a new orphan branch is created with only the
starter files, committed with hooks running.\& Works with any git that has
\fBgit worktree\fR.\& Refuses an existing directory that is not a worktree.\&
The changed \fI.\&gitignore\fR (and \fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR, if written) are left for you to
commit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-message\fR \fIMSG\fR
.RS 4
With \fBsync\fR: commit message, passed to git verbatim.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-push\fR
.RS 4
With \fBsync\fR: push after committing.\& The first push of a new branch sets
its upstream to \fIorigin\fR, or to the only remote.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Show help for the command.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH TASK IDENTIFIERS
A task may carry an identifier: a word on its task line made of `id:` and
four or more lowercase letters and digits, e.\&g.\& `id:k7q2x`.\& It never
changes and is never reused, and it stays with the task when the task is
edited, moved, completed, swept, and archived, so it can be cited from
another task, a commit message, or a review note.\&
.PP
\fBadd\fR and \fBid\fR assign identifiers.\& Each is five characters drawn at random
from \fI/dev/urandom\fR (digits and lowercase letters without i, l, o, and u),
and is redrawn if it already occurs anywhere in \fIactive.\&tm.\&md\fR,
\fIfuture.\&tm.\&md\fR, \fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR, or the archive.\& There is no counter and
no index file.\& An identifier written by hand, or carried over from an
existing scheme (`Z\-0114` as `id:z0114`), is equally valid.\&
.PP
A task names the tasks that must be completed before it can start in a
\fBDepends\fR field, which \fBnext\fR reads:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
\- [ ] +api Add rate limiting id:k7q2x
    > **Depends:** id:m3x8a
.fi
.RE
.PP
Copying a task copies its identifier.\& \fBid\fR and \fBvalidate\fR warn when two
tasks carry the same one; give one of them a new identifier by hand.\&
.PP
.SH TASK HANDLES
\fBlist\fR shows a \fIhandle\fR for each task, e.\&g.\& `[k7q2x]`.\& It is the task'\&s
identifier when the task has one that no other task of the file shares.\&
Otherwise \fBtm\fR derives a deterministic 8\-hex\-digit hash from the task'\&s
summary (the task line minus its checkbox and outer whitespace, so it
survives \fBtm done\fR) and shows its shortest prefix of at least 4 digits that
is unique within the file, e.\&g.\& `[f4a1]`.\& A hash handle is never written to
a file, and editing the task'\&s text changes it.\&
.PP
\fBdone\fR and \fBmove\fR accept:
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
An identifier, with or without its `id:` prefix.\&
.IP \(bu 4
A hash handle, or any longer prefix of the same hash, with or without
brackets.\& A prefix shared by several tasks is rejected, listing each
candidate with its own unique handle.\&
.IP \(bu 4
Otherwise, a case\-insensitive substring of the task summary.\& A substring
matching several tasks is likewise rejected with the candidates listed.\&
.PD
.PP
Two tasks with identical summaries share a hash; make their text differ to
address them separately.\&
.PP
For \fBadd\fR, \fBdone\fR, \fBmove\fR, \fBlist\fR, and \fBnext\fR, `\-\-` ends the options, so task text or
a pattern may begin with '\&\-'\&: `tm add \-\- "\-v flag handling"`.\&
.PP
Task files may be symlinks: \fBtm\fR writes through a link to its target and
leaves the link in place.\&
.PP
.SH FILES
\fI.\&tasks/active.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
The current sprint.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI.\&tasks/future.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
Planned work not yet scheduled to a sprint.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI.\&tasks/completed.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
Strict reverse\-chronological archive of completed work, newest first.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI.\&tasks/archive/<YYYY>/<YYYY\-MM>.\&tm.\&md\fR
.RS 4
Sections aged out of \fIcompleted.\&tm.\&md\fR, newest first.\& Tool\-managed;
never hand\-authored.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI<tasks\-dir>/.\&tm.\&lock\fR
.RS 4
Transient lock directory held by \fBadd\fR, \fBid\fR, \fBdone\fR, \fBmove\fR, \fBremap\fR, \fBsweep\fR,
\fBarchive\fR, and \fBvalidate \-\-fix\fR for the duration of their read\-modify\-write,
so concurrent \fBtm\fR runs wait for each other instead of losing updates.\&
A stale lock left by a killed process may be removed by hand.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration uses a flat `key: value` format, read from two locations, each
optional:
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBGlobal\fR — \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taskmark/config\fR, falling back to
\fI\(ti/.\&config/taskmark/config\fR when unset.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBLocal\fR — \fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR in the current working directory or discovered
by searching upward to the enclosing repository root.\&
.PD
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
tasks_dir: \&.tasks
active_file: active\&.tm\&.md
future_file: future\&.tm\&.md
completed_file: completed\&.tm\&.md
archive_dir: archive
.fi
.RE
.PP
Resolution is per key, highest priority first: an explicit command\-line
option, the local file, the global file, then the built\-in default shown
above.\& When discovered in an ancestor directory, relative paths in
\fI.\&taskmarkrc\fR are resolved relative to the directory containing it.\&
When \fBtasks_dir\fR is not set anywhere and \fI.\&/.\&tasks\fR does not
exist but \fI.\&/doc/tasks\fR (the pre\-0.\&4 default) does, \fI.\&/doc/tasks\fR is used.\&
An absent file, an absent key, or an unparseable line falls back
silently to the next source.\& See \fIdoc/taskmark_spec.\&md\fR §9 for the full
resolution order.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
\fIdoc/taskmark_spec.\&md\fR
.RS 4
The SPEC\-TASKMARK\-05 specification implemented by this tool.\&
.RE
